---
pagination:
  data: themeVocab.concepts
  size: 1
  alias: concept
layout: base.njk
permalink: "/vocab/themes/{{ concept.key }}/index.html"
navKey: "navigator"
lang: en
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ concept.prefLabel.en }}"
  description: "A concept in the European security studies theme vocabulary, tagging {{ concept.count }} papers in the Anthology."
  redirectTo: "{{ concept.pages.en }}"
---
{#- A concept URI has to resolve to something a human can read (#1249). The
    theme's Atlas view is that page, so this is a stub that hands over to it
    and carries the canonical link, rather than a seventeenth thin page
    competing with it in search results. Not the "page moved" body: nothing
    moved, this URI is the concept's permanent name. -#}
<header class="page-header">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="eyebrow">Theme vocabulary</span>
    <h1>{{ concept.prefLabel.en }}</h1>
    <p class="page-lead">
      {{ concept.prefLabel.fr }} · {{ concept.prefLabel.de }}
    </p>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <article class="card" style="padding: clamp(var(--space-6), 2vw + 1rem, var(--space-7));">
      <p>
        This is the permanent identifier for one of the seventeen research
        themes the Anthology indexes by. You'll be taken to the theme's view
        in the Atlas in a moment.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="{{ concept.pages.en }}">{{ concept.prefLabel.en }} in the Atlas</a>
      </p>
      <p class="muted">
        The whole vocabulary, as SKOS:
        <a href="/vocab/themes.ttl">Turtle</a> or
        <a href="/vocab/themes.jsonld">JSON-LD</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
